description: Shepherd project rules (natHacks 2026)
alwaysApply: true
---
Project: Shepherd. Evacuation routing for Edmonton (dashboard + phone web app + FastAPI backend). Hackathon, Defense & Security theme.

Before writing code, read @README.md and @shared/contract.md.

Rules:
- Only edit files inside the folder the user says they are working in. Never touch other folders.
- Never edit shared/contract.md. If it looks wrong, say so.
- Follow the JSON shapes in shared/contract.md exactly.
- GeoJSON coordinates are [lon, lat]. Edmonton is about lon -113.5, lat 53.5.
- Stack: FastAPI (Python 3.11+) backend; Vite + React + maplibre-gl frontends.
- Do not add dependencies without asking.
- No database, no auth, no Docker. State lives in memory.
- Keep code small, simple and readable. Prefer the simplest thing that works.
- Python imports are absolute from repo root, e.g. `from backend.sim.wildfire import WildfireSim`.
- Wildfire is the supported hazard; tornado simulation is a beta feature and must be labelled as beta wherever users see it.
- Backend tests go in the package's `tests/` folder (backend/api/tests, backend/routing/tests, backend/sim/tests).
